help:subtopic.help:semantics:
Add a Gaussian prior centered on rating. The uncertainty is one standard deviation: approximately
68 percent of prior mass lies within plus or minus that value. A zero-like uncertainty becomes a hard anchor;
negative uncertainty is invalid. Extra uncertainty fields are combined in quadrature by v1.2.6, but the three-field form is clearest.

Add a Gaussian prior for rating(Player A) - rating(Player B), centered on
rating_delta with the supplied positive standard deviation. Exactly four fields are required;
a zero or negative uncertainty is rejected.
